   Computing Initiative.

   Source:   https://conceptnet.io
   License:  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
             (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   Because ConceptNet is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (ShareAlike), the
   ConceptNet-derived artifact embedded in this repository remains licensed
   under CC BY-SA 4.0, and any redistribution of that derived data must keep
   it under CC BY-SA 4.0 with attribution. This obligation applies only to the
   ConceptNet-derived data, not to SPIE's own source code.

   Attribution: "ConceptNet" by the Commonsense Computing Initiative,
   used under CC BY-SA 4.0.

2. WordNet (Princeton WordNet)
   ---------------------------
   The deployed service fetches Princeton WordNet at build time; it is not
   stored in this repository. WordNet is a lexical database developed by
   Princeton University.

   Source:   https://wordnet.princeton.edu/
   License:  WordNet License (a permissive BSD-style license) —
             https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use

   Attribution: Princeton University "About WordNet." WordNet. Princeton
   University. 2010.

Open English WordNet (OEWN) is supported as an optional corpus but is NOT
included in, nor fetched by, the default hosted deployment (the server runs
with --no-oewn).
